  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-251",
  "title": "What intrigues you about the cognitive bridge between video data and language?",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What intrigues you about the cognitive bridge between video data and language?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I'm drawn to Eytrix because it's not just building interfaces—it's designing systems that help people *think*. Bridging video and language means creating tools that transform raw perception into structured insight. That challenge intrigues me deeply."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As a front-end developer, I’m especially excited by the idea of crafting someone’s own Sherlock Holmes—a system tuned for pattern recognition, ambient intelligence, and real-time synthesis. Great UX at this level demands close thought about the backend, context, and the subtle cues that make an interface feel intuitive. That intersection of design, cognition, and problem-solving is where I do my best work."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}